\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Settings of the linear examples ($3\times 128$ network, Adam with learning rate $10^{-3}$, early stopping 300/$10^{-5}$). $h$: grid step; $N_{\rm  ep}$: maximal number of epochs per node; start: warm (continuation from the previous node), cold (fresh network), re-init.\ (fresh network every $n$ nodes); $D=\max \ell (E)$ over the window (Corollary\nonbreakingspace \ref {cor.mu}); regime: (ii) faithful ($\mu \ge D^2$), (iii) $\frac  12D^2\le \mu <D^2$, (iv) collapse possible ($\mu <\frac  12D^2$), see Corollary\nonbreakingspace \ref {cor.mu}. Single runs unless the number of seeds is given (seed 0 where the seed was recorded). $^a$Window and step of the accompanying notebook (approximate for the full-scan curves of Figs.\nonbreakingspace \ref {lossNN.fig}, \ref {loss3D.fig}, \ref {pot2.fig}--\ref {fig.well-two}). $^b$Reduced network $3\times 64$, $N=3000$.}}{13}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
